# Git Remote Routing

- Sports arbitrage work belongs in the `sports-arb` GitHub repo (`git@github.com:virtualwriter/sports-arb.git`).
- Broader polymarket-trader work belongs in the original `polymarket-trader` GitHub repo (`git@github.com:virtualwriter/polymarket-trader.git`).
- Before committing or pushing, inspect the changed files and classify the work as sports-arb, polymarket-trader, or mixed.
- If changes are mixed, split them into separate commits and push each commit to the appropriate remote/branch.
- Do not assume the current branch push target is correct for every change. Verify remotes with `git remote -v` and use explicit push targets when needed.
